sup, and prediction markets give her roughly a 70% chance of winning.\n\nThe race has been shaken by a House ethics filing alleging sexual relationships with staffers and hush money payments, which Boebert denies as politically motivated. Challenger Eileen Laubacher has raised over $10 million to Boebert's $1 million and holds a large cash-on-hand edge. With no public polling available, the forecast rests on fundamentals, ratings, and the scandal's trajectory, pointing to a narrowed but still Republican-favored race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}]}